pane-zen-mcp-title = MCP
zen-mcp-server-heading = Built-in MCP server
zen-mcp-description = Connect trusted local clients to control Zen, interact with pages, and use browser developer tools. The server listens only on 127.0.0.1. It is off until you enable it.
zen-mcp-privileged-disclosure = A client with access can execute privileged browser JavaScript without further MCP confirmations. That code can reach private browsing data and saved passwords, even though there are no dedicated tools for them. Grant access only to clients you trust with your browser profile.
zen-mcp-enabled =
    .label = Enable the MCP server
zen-mcp-startup-description = Off by default. When enabled, MCP starts with this browser profile and stops when you turn it off or quit Zen. Installing a connection or skill does not turn it on.
zen-mcp-agents-heading = Connect your agents
zen-mcp-agents-description = Set up a local MCP connection for Codex or Claude Code. Each button creates separate client access and saves the token in that client's configuration on this computer. An existing connection installed by Zen is replaced; other connections are preserved. Restart the agent after setup.
zen-mcp-connect-codex =
    .label = Set up Codex MCP
zen-mcp-connect-claude =
    .label = Set up Claude Code MCP
zen-mcp-agents-manual-description = For manual setup, create a named client below. Its one-time panel includes the address, bearer token, JSON, Codex TOML and terminal commands for both clients. Codex automatic setup requires its CLI. If a configuration was edited outside Zen, use the manual option.
zen-mcp-skills-heading = Browser skill
zen-mcp-skills-description = Install instructions for using Zen's MCP in ~/.agents/skills (Codex) or ~/.claude/skills (Claude Code). Skills contain no access tokens. Playground installs its own skill and connection. Edited or unrelated skills are preserved. Reopen the agent if the skill does not appear.
zen-mcp-install-codex-skill =
    .label = Install skill for Codex
zen-mcp-install-claude-skill =
    .label = Install skill for Claude Code
zen-mcp-open-codex-skills =
    .label = Open Codex skills
zen-mcp-agent-connected = MCP connection saved to { $path }. Enable the server above to accept connections.
zen-mcp-skill-installed = Browser skill installed at { $path }.
zen-mcp-error-connect-codex = Could not set up Codex. Install the Codex CLI and check ~/.codex/config.toml. An existing connection named zen (zen_playground in Playground), an edited Zen block, or a changed file may prevent setup. Use a named client below for manual configuration.
zen-mcp-error-connect-claude = Could not set up Claude Code. Check ~/.claude.json. An existing connection named zen (zen_playground in Playground), an edited connection, or a changed file may prevent setup. Use a named client below for manual configuration.
zen-mcp-error-install-skill = Could not install the skill. Check access to the skills folder. Zen will not overwrite an unrelated or edited skill; keep your version or move it before installing.
zen-mcp-error-open-codex = Could not open Codex. Install the desktop app, then open its Skills section.
zen-mcp-status-unavailable = Server status is unavailable.
zen-mcp-status-disabled = The MCP server is off.
zen-mcp-status-stopped = The MCP server is enabled but is not listening.
zen-mcp-status-running = The MCP server is listening.
zen-mcp-instance-main = This is your main Zen instance. Its access grants belong to this profile.
zen-mcp-instance-playground = This is Zen Playground. Its access grants are independent of your main browser.
zen-mcp-server-error = Server error: { $error }
zen-mcp-port-label = Port
zen-mcp-port-hint = Leave the port empty to use the default ({ $port }). Valid ports are 1–65535.
zen-mcp-apply-port =
    .label = Apply port
zen-mcp-endpoint-label = Local HTTP endpoint
zen-mcp-copy-endpoint =
    .label = Copy address
zen-mcp-refresh =
    .label = Refresh status
zen-mcp-clients-heading = Trusted clients
zen-mcp-clients-description = Create a separate access token for each client. You can create access while the server is off. Replacing a token invalidates the old one; revoking access immediately disconnects the client.
zen-mcp-client-name-label = Client name
zen-mcp-add-client =
    .label = Create access
zen-mcp-clients-empty = No clients have access yet.
zen-mcp-client-created = Created: { DATETIME($createdAt, dateStyle: "medium", timeStyle: "short") }
zen-mcp-client-created-unknown = Creation time is unavailable.
zen-mcp-client-last-used = Last used: { DATETIME($lastUsedAt, dateStyle: "medium", timeStyle: "short") }
zen-mcp-client-unused = Not used yet.
zen-mcp-client-rotate =
    .label = Replace token
zen-mcp-client-revoke =
    .label = Revoke access
zen-mcp-grant-heading = Access for { $name }
zen-mcp-grant-description = Save this token or copy a connection configuration now. Zen stores only its hash and cannot show it again. This panel clears the token when you leave this section or close settings. The configurations below also contain the token.
zen-mcp-token-label = Bearer token
zen-mcp-copy-token =
    .label = Copy token
zen-mcp-json-config-label = JSON connection configuration
zen-mcp-copy-json =
    .label = Copy JSON
zen-mcp-codex-config-label = Codex configuration (~/.codex/config.toml)
zen-mcp-copy-codex =
    .label = Copy Codex TOML
zen-mcp-codex-command-label = Codex CLI command (macOS / Linux terminal)
zen-mcp-codex-command-description = This command uses a token environment variable in the current terminal. For the desktop app or a persistent connection, use Set up Codex MCP or the TOML above. Commands contain the token; keep them private.
zen-mcp-copy-codex-command =
    .label = Copy Codex command
zen-mcp-claude-command-label = Claude Code CLI command (macOS / Linux terminal)
zen-mcp-copy-claude-command =
    .label = Copy Claude Code command
zen-mcp-dismiss-grant =
    .label = Clear token from this panel
zen-mcp-copied = Copied to the clipboard.
zen-mcp-error-initialize = Could not initialize MCP settings. Refresh the status to try again.
zen-mcp-error-refresh = Could not read the MCP server status. Refresh the status to try again.
zen-mcp-error-enable = Could not change the MCP server state. Check the server status before trying again.
zen-mcp-error-port = Enter a whole port number from 1 to 65535, or leave it empty for the default.
zen-mcp-error-apply-port = Could not change the port. Check the server status before trying again.
zen-mcp-error-name = Enter a client name with 1–100 characters and no control characters.
zen-mcp-error-open-pane = Could not open the MCP section. Open it from the sidebar before creating or replacing access.
zen-mcp-error-create = Could not complete access creation. Check the client list before trying again; replace the token if access was created but its token is unavailable.
zen-mcp-error-rotate = Could not complete token replacement. Check the client list before trying again.
zen-mcp-error-revoke = Could not complete access revocation. Check the client list before trying again.
zen-mcp-error-copy = Could not copy to the clipboard. Select and copy the value manually.
